import{_ as o,o as t,c as s,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.BN3Eol-0.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"UXD-038 — One length rule for the long text pages: first 10 + \\"Show all N\\", a colophon totals line, launcher sketches apart from the spacecraft cutaways","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-038-one-length-rule-for-the-long-text-pages.md","filePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-038-one-length-rule-for-the-long-text-pages.md"}'),c={name:"uxs/decisions/UXD-038-one-length-rule-for-the-long-text-pages.md"};function n(r,e,i,d,l,h){return t(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="uxd-038-—-one-length-rule-for-the-long-text-pages-first-10-show-all-n-a-colophon-totals-line-launcher-sketches-apart-from-the-spacecraft-cutaways" tabindex="-1">UXD-038 — One length rule for the long text pages: first 10 + &quot;Show all N&quot;, a colophon totals line, launcher sketches apart from the spacecraft cutaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#uxd-038-—-one-length-rule-for-the-long-text-pages-first-10-show-all-n-a-colophon-totals-line-launcher-sketches-apart-from-the-spacecraft-cutaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;UXD-038 — One length rule for the long text pages: first 10 + &quot;Show all N&quot;, a colophon totals line, launcher sketches apart from the spacecraft cutaways&quot;">​</a></h1><ul><li><strong>Status</strong>: accepted (built; checked by unit tests, e2e on three projects and screenshots, not yet by the operator)</li><li><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-11-14</li><li><strong>Decider</strong>: the operator, 2026-11-14 — &quot;I&#39;m okay with all the recommendations. Go for them.&quot; (the recommendations of <code>docs/wip/2026-11-14-slice-F1-brief.md</code> §12: decisions 24a, 26a, 27a, 28a; 25a is slice F2&#39;s)</li><li><strong>Answers</strong>: CR2, CR3, CO1, CO2, CO3 of the UX feedback plan; Q7 and Q9; slice F1 (CR1 was closed by A2)</li><li><strong>Builds on</strong>: <a href="./UXD-012-one-page-shell">UXD-012</a> (the page shell), <a href="./UXD-014-one-chip-and-filter">UXD-014</a> (&quot;Show all&quot; is the one action chip)</li><li><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/lib/preview-list.ts</code> (+ test), <code>src/lib/components/ShowAll.svelte</code>, <code>src/lib/colophon-sections.ts</code> (+ test), <code>src/routes/credits/+page.svelte</code>, <code>src/routes/colophon/+page.svelte</code>, <code>scripts/build-original-work.mjs</code> and <code>static/data/original-work.json</code> (<code>kind</code> on each cutaway), <code>static/data/schemas/original-work.schema.json</code>, <code>src/lib/image-sizes.ts</code> (<code>colophonPortrait</code>), <code>src/lib/credits-coverage.test.ts</code>, <code>scripts/audit-scene-image-credits.mjs</code>, <code>tests/e2e/image-weight.spec.ts</code> (budgets, ready selector), <code>messages/*.json</code> (<code>colophon_section_launchers</code>, <code>colophon_totals</code>), <code>tests/e2e/colophon.spec.ts</code> (new), <code>tests/e2e/credits.spec.ts</code>. No image, no provenance row and no overlay file changed.</li></ul><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>CR2 / CO2.</strong> <code>/credits</code> drew every row of 42 sources (3185 photo rows, 54 text rows, 110 insignia, 69 video posters, 29 data entries; 3,393 images in the DOM) and carried a 43 MB image budget on every device. <code>/colophon</code> already showed 10 items per section and a &quot;Show all&quot; chip, which took it from 62.7 MB to 4.1 MB on a phone (2026-11-08).</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>One rule for every long list (24a).</strong> A list draws its first <code>PREVIEW</code> = 10 rows (<code>previewList</code> in <code>$lib/preview-list</code>) and, while longer and not opened, a &quot;Show all N&quot; chip (<code>ShowAll</code>, an <code>action</code> <code>Chip</code>; text <code>colophon_show_all</code>). The source and section headers stay open. The opened state is runtime only (no storage). <code>/credits</code> applies it to every source&#39;s photo list and text list, the audio, video and insignia lists and the data catalogues; <code>/colophon</code> replaces its page-local <code>shown()</code> and snippet with the same two parts. The 69 video posters are <code>loading=&quot;lazy&quot;</code> again: the cap removed the reason they were eager.</li><li><strong>Anchors and Ctrl-F.</strong> A contents link (<code>#src-&lt;id&gt;</code>, <code>#sec-&lt;id&gt;</code>) lands on an open header with its first 10 rows below it, so no hash handler is needed. &quot;Show all&quot; sits at the foot of the list: the rows are inserted below the chip, so the first new row opens where the chip was (<code>credits.spec.ts</code> asserts the 11th row is in view after the click; scrollY itself moves by the browser&#39;s scroll anchoring when off-screen <code>content-visibility</code> blocks above settle to their real height, which is why it is not the thing asserted). Ctrl-F finds text in the rows that are drawn; a row beyond the tenth is found after &quot;Show all&quot;, the cost of a cap that the closed-section alternative (24b) would have shared.</li><li><strong>The <code>/credits</code> contents list</strong> (42 rows, 1,578 px high on a phone) is capped the same way below 768 px only (<code>ShowAll narrow</code> with <code>class=&quot;preview-narrow&quot;</code> on the list, the rule in <code>ShowAll.svelte</code>); from 768 px it sits in two columns and stays whole. <code>/colophon</code>&#39;s contents list (16 rows) is not capped. <code>/library</code> follows the rule in F2 (25a).</li><li><strong>Colophon totals line (27a).</strong> <code>colophonSections()</code> in <code>$lib/colophon-sections</code> returns the sections the page draws, in page order, with their counts; the contents list, the heading counts and the line &quot;N original works in K sections&quot; (<code>colophon_totals</code>, <code>data-testid=&quot;colophon-totals&quot;</code>, under the lead) read those rows, never the manifest&#39;s <code>totals</code> object, which leaves out the tour episodes and the icon grid. Interface graphics: the contents row said 4 (<code>data.ui</code>) and its heading 14 (the glyph registry); both now read the registry. The contents list now follows the page order (posters came before the mission trajectories in the page and after them in the list).</li><li><strong>Launcher sketches (26a).</strong> Each <code>anatomy_art</code> entry has <code>kind: &#39;spacecraft&#39; | &#39;launcher&#39;</code>, set by <code>build-original-work.mjs</code>: <code>launcher</code> when the fleet entry&#39;s category is <code>launcher</code>, plus two drawings with no fleet entry (<code>m-v</code>, <code>pslv</code>) named in the script. 158 spacecraft cutaways and 40 launcher sketches (portrait 2:3 pencil, drawn as their own section with portrait cards, <code>colophon_section_launchers</code>); the exploded section keeps its 76. A <code>kind</code> field leaves every translated overlay (keyed by file) where it is. <code>colophon-sections.test.ts</code> fails on a new drawing that has no fleet entry until the script&#39;s list is looked at.</li><li><strong>Moon, Mars and Earth credits (28a).</strong> <code>src/lib/credits-coverage.test.ts</code> fails when an image file under the Moon, Mars or Earth scene folders has no row in <code>image-provenance.json</code> (matched by stem as <code>/credits</code> bundles; a width rung is told from a name ending in digits by <code>image-ladder.json</code>). <code>scripts/audit-scene-image-credits.mjs</code> is the browser audit: it loads the three scenes and their first sites and compares every requested image to the manifest. A row is not a verified credit: the 71 placeholder credits stay on the repo&#39;s own ceiling (<code>validate-gallery-credits</code>).</li></ol><h2 id="verification" tabindex="-1">Verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Unit: <code>preview-list.test.ts</code>, <code>colophon-sections.test.ts</code> (158 + 40 = 198 cutaways, launchers = the fleet&#39;s launchers plus <code>m-v</code> and <code>pslv</code>, the exploded 76 whole), <code>credits-coverage.test.ts</code> (9 folders, mutation-checked: adding <code>images/landing-sequences</code> makes it fail with 39 files), <code>validate-data</code>, <code>npm run check</code> (0 errors).</p><p>E2E on desktop-chromium, mobile-chromium and mobile-landscape-chromium against the dev server, <code>--workers=1</code>: <code>credits.spec.ts</code> (13) and the new <code>colophon.spec.ts</code> (4: the totals line equals the sum of the section counts on screen, the contents rows equal the headings, 158 / 40 / 76, Show all opens the rest, a contents link lands on its header with 10 rows below); on desktop-chromium also the <code>a11y</code>, <code>type-floor</code>, <code>chip</code>, <code>page-shell</code>, <code>accent-colour</code>, <code>smoke</code> and <code>video-media</code> rows of the two pages. Dev-server hydration timeouts and 500s in the first runs were rerun alone and passed.</p><p>Image weight after a full scroll (<code>image-weight.spec.ts</code>, dev server, not a production build): <code>/credits</code> 40.8 MB on a phone with every &quot;Show all&quot; opened (the old rendering, 3,393 images in the DOM) and 3.7 / 3.7 / 3.7 / 3.7 MB (phone / tablet / desktop / tv) as built (308 images), oversize 0; the budget moves from 43 to 5 on all four. <code>/colophon</code> is 5.0 / 5.0 / 2.9 / 4.8 MB (was 4.1 / 4.1 / 2.6 / 3.9 on 2026-11-08; not attributed between the launcher section and the art added since), so its budget moves from 5 / 5 / 3 / 5 to 6 / 6 / 4 / 6. The spec now waits for the page&#39;s own sources to render before it reads: before, a slow dev-server hydration read ~0 MB and passed.</p><p>CR3: <code>scripts/audit-scene-image-credits.mjs --sites=5</code> against the dev server (each scene and its first five sites, every panel tab opened): <code>/moon</code> 105 image requests, 72 stems; <code>/mars</code> 43, 30; <code>/earth</code> 51, 31; all credited on <code>/credits</code> or listed as Orrery&#39;s own art on <code>/colophon</code>; 0 with no credit, 0 external, 0 failed. A lower bound: a request the run did not trigger (a site beyond the fifth, a gallery image past the first tab) is not seen.</p><p>Not checked: Firefox and WebKit; Ctrl-F behaviour was reasoned, not tried; a production build; the other 13 locales&#39; pages (the two keys and their numbers were not looked at on screen); whether each credit row is right, not only present.</p>',12)])])}const g=o(c,[["render",n]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
